// Applied inside the NemoClaw sandbox by `scripts/nemoclaw-setup.sh config` (it fills in __PUBLIC_HOST__ from .env):
//   openclaw config patch --stdin   (run as the sandbox user)
// openclaw.json is authoritative after first launch, survives restarts, and `nemoclaw rebuild` restores it.
//
// Only the public address of the Control UI is set here. Leave `gateway.auth` alone: NemoClaw's start script rewrites the gateway
// token on every container start, and OpenClaw refuses `trusted-proxy` auth while a token is configured, so SSO into OpenClaw
// is not possible with NemoClaw 0.0.137. Authelia gates the URL; the browser also needs the gateway token and a paired device.
//
// The model, provider and inference route are written by `nemoclaw onboard`; there is deliberately no `agents` block.
{
  gateway: {
    publicOrigin: "https://__PUBLIC_HOST__",
    controlUi: {
      basePath: "/openclaw",
      allowedOrigins: ["http://127.0.0.1:18789", "https://__PUBLIC_HOST__"],
    },
  },
}
